  "description": "This dataset comprises high-density and sparse functional near-infrared spectroscopy (fNIRS) measurements acquired during a Word-Color Stroop task from 10 participants. The study investigates whether high-density multi-distance fNIRS configurations enhance detection of brain activity compared to conventional sparse probe arrangements. Data include raw fNIRS signals suitable for cognitive neuroscience research on executive function and conflict processing.",
  "methods_description": "Functional near-infrared spectroscopy data were acquired during a Word-Color Stroop task using both high-density and sparse fNIRS probe configurations. Measurements include multi-distance fNIRS signals capturing hemodynamic responses. This study compares high-density probe arrangements with conventional sparse configurations to evaluate differences in brain activity detection.",
